The deeper bet
<p>In a software-scarce world, owning code mattered.</p>
<p>In an intelligence-abundant world, the scarce layer becomes:</p>
<p><strong>proof that the physical world is actually in state X and that ac=
tion Y actually worked.</strong></p>
<p>A future superhuman agent can infer a lot.</p>
<p>It cannot infer the exact failure history that nobody recorded.</p>
<p>It cannot reconstruct stock snapshots nobody archived.</p>
<p>It cannot know a printer=E2=80=99s real MTBF by configuration if nobody =
collected telemetry.</p>
<p>It cannot recover a decade of component scarcity history after the fact.=
</p>
<p>It cannot recreate physical experience from software alone.</p>
<p>That is the garden.</p>

